## GitHub overlay image build proposal

- Frozen OpenSpec package `add-github-overlay-image-build` for building the
  fork image from GitHub and pulling it on the server. Docker construction and
  backend compilation run only on a canonical `main` push or manual dispatch
  selected on exact main. PR/feature checks are ordinary unit, OpenSpec,
  workflow-syntax, and static checks only; they do not build Docker, compile
  the backend, or publish. The main workflow uses the existing official
  UI/backend overlay and pinned ARM64 base digest
  `sha256:754b5e50361dc2802f0b6576456e72a5163cdc991378ce3f212a2f90b771eb96`,
  verifies one local candidate before GHCR authentication, and publishes the
  full-SHA and `:main` tags with recorded manifest digest and source/base/run
  metadata. The operator pulls the main image, compares its digest, starts
  with `docker compose up -d --no-build`, and retains prior-digest rollback.
- The smoke contract targets the direct Next UI listener (`20128`):
  unauthenticated `GET /api/v1/models` returns HTTP 401 with
  `error.code: "invalid_api_key"`. This is the route-handler response;
  `AUTH_002` is generated by the separate API-listener proxy and is not the
  candidate's direct UI response.
- Proposal, design, tasks, capability delta, and repo TODO track the same
  main-only trigger and acceptance policy. The PR must include reviewed runtime
  changes and eligible completed OpenSpec archives. GHCR's first publication
  defaults private; after a successful main publish, the owner switches the
  package to public and anonymous pull is verified. The workflow leaves
  visibility unchanged. Automated production deployment is separate follow-up
  scope.
- Implementation is complete on the feature branch. Focused verification
  passed 12/12 tests (9 new policy/verifier/Compose and freshness tests plus 3
  manifest-merger tests), ESLint, Prettier, actionlint, the workflow-security
  ratchet (210 findings versus 233 at baseline), strict OpenSpec validation
  (7/7), and `git diff --check`. Independent low-effort code review reported
  no findings. Code Simplifier removed redundant `Promise.all` usage, reused
  fixtures, and made the expected digest explicit.
- The local Docker daemon did not respond, so no Docker image build or
  Docker-backed candidate acceptance ran. CI commit
  `38cae506dcfb54a4e01fb5b4828fbd37b29e4d18` is created locally; feature push
  and PR are pending. No GitHub Actions run, image publication, or production
  change has occurred.
  The review PR must include the runtime work and eligible completed archives;
  pre-merge checks remain required. After merge, the actual native ARM64 main
  build is the next image gate. Then publish/record digest, switch the package
  public, verify anonymous pull, and complete server health and rollback
  acceptance. Audit branch/main/deployed-base history before opening the PR;
  do not restore legacy fork-only behavior without a reviewed requirement.
  Keep automated production deployment as separate future scope.
- Pre-PR history audit: remote `main` is `f2bddef27ed0807dd5a5e2712bc26536edda8138`; feature is `11a54874b7e236df5935e54f17a7ffcb5564d88d`; deployed runtime source is `55f40468137290e8efdc24a1a1b95b111a61d91a`. The reviewed feature tree follows official upstream v3.8.52 and its diff against current `main` spans 1,147 files (40,769 additions, 22,230 deletions), including the upstream sync and intentional removal of legacy fork-only web-fetch/search/routing/FMO behavior. Preserve the exact current main SHA on a new archive ref before integrating its ancestry; describe the broad upstream delta in the PR.
- Read-only GitHub settings: Actions enabled, allowed actions `all`, default workflow token permission `write`; the new workflow uses narrower explicit permissions. No main branch protection or repo/inherited rulesets are configured, so manually verify PR review and green static checks before merge. GHCR has no `omniroute` package yet. After first publish, make it public in GitHub Packages UI and verify anonymous pull; official REST/GraphQL surfaces no package-visibility mutation, and public cannot be reverted to private.
- Fresh main archive is pushed and verified: `archive/main-before-main-image-pr-2026-10-03` points to `f2bddef27ed0807dd5a5e2712bc26536edda8138`; `main` remained at that SHA through the pre-integration fetch. The feature records this `main` history with an ours-strategy merge, retaining the reviewed upstream-aligned source tree.
